---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Developers" description="Build on your Portico server with the server API, scoped API keys, signed webhooks and an MCP endpoint, plus guides to authentication and client architecture.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="type-mega">Build with Portico.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Portico's own apps use the same server API you can. Create a scoped API key, script your library, receive signed webhooks, or connect an assistant over MCP. All of it runs on your own server, with no Portico Account required.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/developers/api/">Start an integration</a>
        <a class="button button-ghost" href="/docs/developers/api-overview/">API architecture overview</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="band" aria-label="What you can build">
    <div class="container">
      <ul class="capabilities capabilities-four" role="list">
        <li>
          <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 4c-2 0-3 1-3 3v2c0 1.5-.8 2.5-2 3 1.2.5 2 1.5 2 3v2c0 2 1 3 3 3M16 4c2 0 3 1 3 3v2c0 1.5.8 2.5 2 3-1.2.5-2 1.5-2 3v2c0 2-1 3-3 3" /></svg></span>
          <h3>Server API</h3>
          <p>The server API under <code>/v1</code> on port 32500, described by a published OpenAPI contract: libraries, search, playback, Live TV, DVR and metadata.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="15" r="4" /><path d="m11 12 9-9M17 6l3 3M14.5 8.5l2.5 2.5" /></svg></span>
          <h3>API keys and tokens</h3>
          <p>Create scoped keys under Settings → Server → Integrations. Send one as a bearer header from your tool or script.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7Z" /></svg></span>
          <h3>Signed webhooks</h3>
          <p>The server posts events straight to your endpoint, signed with HMAC-SHA256, with retries and a delivery log.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v11H9l-5 4Z" /><path d="M8.5 10.5h.01M12 10.5h.01M15.5 10.5h.01" /></svg></span>
          <h3>Assistants</h3>
          <p>A Model Context Protocol endpoint at <code>/v1/mcp</code>. Tools follow the key's scopes and the member's permissions.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="type-d2 dev-heading">Two APIs, two jobs.</h2>
      <div class="split-panels">
        <article>
          <h3>Portico Server</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Media and libraries</li>
            <li>Playback decisions and streams</li>
            <li>Server accounts and permissions</li>
            <li>Server administration</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Portico Services</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Portico Accounts and sign-in security</li>
            <li>Server membership and invitations</li>
            <li>Signed route discovery for direct connections</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
      <h2 class="type-d2 dev-heading">Guides and reference.</h2>
      <div class="developer-grid">
        <a href="/developers/api/clients/"><strong>Building a Portico app</strong><span>The full generated reference for client applications.</span></a>
        <a href="/developers/api/"><strong>Integrations</strong><span>Small task guides, tool setup and the native Integrations reference.</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/developers/api-overview/"><strong>API architecture overview</strong><span>Choose the Server API or the Portico Services API and see where each one's authentication applies.</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/developers/authentication/"><strong>Authentication</strong><span>Sign people in, keep sessions safe and use API keys.</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/developers/client-architecture/"><strong>Client architecture</strong><span>Follow the shared client behaviour and use each platform's native playback.</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/developers/security-requirements/"><strong>Security requirements</strong><span>Verify direct routes, respect server permissions and keep credentials out of logs and URLs you share.</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/developers/reporting-issues/"><strong>Report an issue</strong><span>Send useful evidence without exposing media, credentials or private addresses.</span></a>
        <a href="/docs/security/report-a-security-issue/"><strong>Report a security issue</strong><span>Tell us privately about a vulnerability.</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
